{
  "name": "Turn inbound email into a workflow (no mail server) — Webhook Relay",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 📧 Turn inbound email into a workflow — no mail server\n\n**Who's it for**\nTeams that want to trigger automations from **email** (support inboxes, alerts, order confirmations, parsing) without running or exposing a mail server — and without exposing n8n itself.\n\n**What it does**\n[Webhook Relay](https://webhookrelay.com) gives you a real inbound email address, parses each message to JSON (from, subject, text/html, attachments, and SPF/DKIM/DMARC results) and streams it to n8n over an **outbound WebSocket**. n8n stays on localhost / behind NAT and never listens for inbound connections.\n\n**How it works**\n1. **Email Trigger** receives the parsed message over the socket.\n2. **Parse email** pulls out the fields you care about.\n3. **Passed DKIM check?** verifies the sender isn't spoofed.\n4. **Forward verified email** POSTs it to your endpoint; unverified mail is flagged.\n\n**Setup (2 min)**\n1. Install the community node: **Settings → Community Nodes → Install** → `n8n-nodes-webhookrelay`.\n2. Add a **Webhook Relay API** credential — API key from [my.webhookrelay.com/tokens](https://my.webhookrelay.com/tokens).\n3. Open the trigger's **Email Address** field to load your inbound address.\n4. (Optional) restrict **Allowed Senders**, then **Activate** and email that address.",
        "height": 520,
        "width": 640,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "bb000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-160, 60]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 1 · Receive email — no mail server\nOpen **Email Address** on this node to get your inbound address. Every message sent to it is parsed to JSON and streamed here.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 260,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "bb000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "Section: receive",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [540, 640]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 2 · Parse & verify\n**Parse email** extracts the useful fields. **Passed DKIM check?** is an example anti-spoofing gate — legitimate senders that sign their mail pass; forged senders don't.\n\n✏️ Adjust the check (or use SPF/DMARC) to fit your senders.",
        "height": 440,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "bb000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "Section: parse",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [840, 560]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "### 3 · Act — edit these\n✏️ Point **Forward verified email** at your own endpoint (Slack/Discord webhook, a ticketing API, Google Sheets…). Unverified mail hits a No-Op — replace it with your own quarantine/alert step.",
        "height": 440,
        "width": 340,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "bb000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "Section: act",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1400, 560]
    },
